libwavpack: arithmetic on the samples of a corrupt block wraps rather than overflows

A block decodes to whatever its bits say, and a corrupt one hands the decorrelation samples, weights and corrections of any size, whose sums, differences and products then overflow int32_t, which C leaves undefined. The code was written for the wrap that two's complement arithmetic gives -- the CRC and the mute limit catch what comes out -- and upstream's fuzzing build turns the check for it off (fuzzing/build.sh), but a compiler may assume the overflow never happens. MediaPerch's WavPack fuzzers, built for Linux with UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer, found it in one night at two places, the term-18 prediction of decorr_mono_pass and the joint stereo of unpack_samples, and a build of the decoder without the assembly, run over the fuzzers' corpora and upstream's regression files, reached 40 operations on 22 lines: every term of decorr_mono_pass and all but term -1 of decorr_stereo_pass, apply_weight, the joint stereo, and the negation of a float's magnitude in both loops of unpack_floats.c. wavpack_local.h now has wrap_add, wrap_sub, wrap_mul and wrap_neg, which compute in uint32_t and hand back the int32_t with the same bits; apply_weight_i, apply_weight_f and update_weight are written with them, and so are the sums of unpack_samples -- lossless, hybrid lossy and hybrid lossless with its cross decorrelation and its noise shaping --, of decorr_mono_pass and decorr_stereo_pass, and the two negations. fixup_samples makes the additions it made in int32_t in uint32_t, where it already made the shifts after them, and the mute limit is compared with llabs(), since labs() of the one sample -2^31 overflows where long has 32 bits, as on Windows. For a block that decodes correctly nothing overflows and every value is what it was, and for a corrupt one every value is what the processors made of it before: over 9,463 files -- 288 made by the wavpack program from twelve WAV files in twenty-four modes, 144 of them with a correction file, then the fuzzers' corpora and findings and upstream's regression files, which between them reach every line this changes -- the patched decoder gives the same samples as the original compiled with -fwrapv, and under UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer reports nothing where the original reported those 40, in the same time. The variants PERFCOND leaves out are unchanged. Against 5.9.0-56-gb0e6c05.

